From 2a9aabca057a77fddde2ec75cd81c3ee8dd9fd9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:46:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Cache eCash header SHA256 midstate for WebGPU nonce search

Factor SHA256 compression out of the CPU reference and compute the first unpadded 64-byte header block once per worker job. Key the cache by the exact prefix and pass its eight state words to the SHA256d shader. Each nonce now executes the remaining first-hash block and the second hash through one compression primitive.

Preserve serialized header bytes, digest byte order, target comparisons, native BLAKE3 mining and worker cancellation. Add independent OpenSSL differential checks, randomized nonce/prefix and target-boundary cases, and opt-in GPU coverage.
